.TH FATHOM_NOTE_WITHDRAW 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-note\-withdraw \- Take a recorded decision back, by appending the note that retracts it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom note withdraw\fR [\fB\-\-author\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> <\fITEXT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Take a recorded decision back, by appending the note that retracts it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-author\fR \fI<AUTHOR>\fR
Who is retracting it
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\fR \fI<AGENT>\fR
Record the retraction as an agent\*(Aqs act on someone\*(Aqs behalf
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
The note being retracted (`nt\-…`)
.TP
<\fITEXT\fR>
Why it no longer holds
